@startuml pipeline
title The three stages — what each one is allowed to know

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333333

|#F5F5F5|EXTRACTION|
start
:downstream user writes
""#[configuration(colour(Red), name = "thing")]"" ;
note right
  arrives as ""syn::DeriveInput""
end note

:**walk** to the nodes;
note right
  Answers exactly two questions:
  * what is the SOURCE of this extraction? → ""Sourced""
  * how do we GET THERE? → ""Visitable""

  Never answers "how should this be parsed".
end note

:**carry** what it finds;
note right
  May hand on raw tokens.
  ""Unresolved<'ast, T>"" is the carrier.
end note

:surface-level ""Validate"" only;
note right
  does this exist where required?
  is this value within a bound?
  — NOT parsing, NOT grammar
  (#pipeline/validity-scope)
end note

:emit ""Extracted<T, I>"";
note right
  Output is UNBOUNDED on the trait.
  Source rides on the OUTPUT so it
  survives a failed extraction, where
  there is no T to ask.
end note

|#FFF4E5|PROCESSING|
:receive ""Extracted<T, I>"" **whole**;
note right
  The pipeline does NOT unwrap between
  stages — unwrapping would strip the
  source off exactly the value that
  needs it.
end note

:**understand** the tokens;
note right
  ""Meta"" → openings → grammar types.
  THIS is where a ""ColourSetting"" is
  read out of a ""Meta"". It is NOT
  extraction — putting it there was a
  stage-boundary violation.
end note

:accumulate ""Reason""s — never abort;
note right
  no ""?"", no early return, so no way
  to drop a sibling (#no-result)
end note

|#E8F4EA|GENERATION|
:**splice** selectors verbatim;
note right
  ""#[shape(AttributeKind::MetaList)]""
  goes into a TYPE position and rustc
  resolves it. Never parsed by us.
end note

:re-emit keys as a struct literal;
note right
  hands UnknownKey / Missing / Duplicate
  to rustc, with did-you-mean
end note

:emit stub impl **alongside** errors;
note right
  or the missing impl cascades into
  "does not implement" at every use
  site and buries the real diagnostic
end note
stop

@enduml
